": {"date-parts": [[2016, 5, 27]]}, "article-number": "052119"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 30]], "date-time": "2026-07-30T16:01:07Z", "timestamp": 1785427267513, "version": "3.56.0"}, "reference-count": 39, "publisher": "American Physical Society (APS)", "issue": "4", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 13]], "date-time": "2025-11-13T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1762992000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/100000925", "name": "John Templeton Foundation", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100000925", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100000923", "name": "Silicon Valley Community Foundation", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["FQXi-RFP-CPW-2008"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["FQXi-RFP-CPW-2008"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100000923", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100000923", "name": "Silicon Valley Community Foundation", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["FQXi-MGB-2011"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["FQXi-MGB-2011"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100000923", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100009566", "name": "Foundational Questions Institute", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100009566", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100000780", "name": "European Commission", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["CA23115"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["CA23115"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100000780", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100000780", "name": "European Commission", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["CA23130"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["CA23130"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100000780", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100014144", "name": "Museo Storico della Fisica e Centro Studi e Ricerche Enrico Fermi", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100014144", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["journals.aps.org"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Phys. Rev. Research"], "accepted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 31]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Models of spontaneous wavefunction collapse explain the quantum-to-classical transition without invoking the von Neumann measurement postulate. Prominent frameworks, such as the Diósi-Penrose (DP) and continuous spontaneous localization (CSL) models, propose a continuous, spontaneous measurement of the mass density field of quantized matter. We show that this mechanism could link both models—not just DP—to fundamental uncertainties in Newtonian gravity. Despite their nonrelativistic nature, these models suggest an induced uncertainty in the flow of time due to fluctuations in the Newtonian potential. We calculate the ultimate limit on time uncertainty and demonstrate that the resulting clock-time uncertainty remains negligible for all contemporary timekeeping devices, including atomic clocks.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1103/p6tj-lg8l", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 31]], "date-time": "2025-07-31T15:44:19Z", "timestamp": 1753976659000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1103/crossmark-policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Fundamental limits on clock precision from spacetime uncertainty in quantum collapse models"], "prefix": "10.1103", "volume": "7", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9344-3657", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Nicola", "family": "Bortolotti", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"id": [{"id": "https://ror.org/01qb1sw63", "id-type": "ROR", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "name": "Centro Ricerche Enrico Fermi"}, {"id": [{"id": "https://ror.org/02be6w209", "id-type": "ROR", "asserted-by": "